---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Ultimate Guide to Secure & Private PDF Merging Offline";
const description = "Learn why merging PDFs offline in your browser is the safest way to handle sensitive documents. Free, no-upload PDF tools explained.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} active="tools" canonicalPath="/guides/secure-pdf-merging-offline">
    <section class="page-header">
        <div class="container">
            <h1>Secure & Private PDF Merging</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">Why your documents should never leave your device.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <div class="container container-narrow">
            <article class="prose">
                <p>When you merge PDFs online using traditional tools, your files are uploaded to a remote server. This poses a significant security risk, especially if the documents contain sensitive information like PAN cards, Aadhar numbers, or bank statements.</p>
                
                <h2>The Privacy Risk of Online PDF Tools</h2>
                <p>Many "free" tools monetize your data or have lax security protocols. Once a document is uploaded, you lose control over who can see it or where it's stored. Even if they promise to delete it, the risk of a data breach is always present.</p>
                
                <h2>The FormFix Way: 100% Client-Side</h2>
                <p>FormFix uses modern web technologies (WebAssembly and JavaScript) to process your PDFs directly in your browser. This means:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>No Server Uploads:</strong> Your files never travel across the internet.</li>
                    <li><strong>Instant Processing:</strong> No waiting for uploads or downloads from a server.</li>
                    <li><strong>Works Offline:</strong> Once the page is loaded, you can even disconnect your internet and it still works.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>How to Merge PDFs Safely</h2>
                <ol>
                    <li>Open the <a href="/merge-pdf">PDF Merger</a> on FormFix.</li>
                    <li>Select the PDF files you want to combine.</li>
                    <li>Arrange them in your preferred order.</li>
                    <li>Click <strong>Merge PDF</strong>.</li>
                    <li>The combined file is generated in your browser memory instantly.</li>
                </ol>

                <div class="mt-32">
                    <p>Stop risking your sensitive data. Switch to a privacy-first toolkit.</p>
                    <a href="/merge-pdf" class="primary-btn">Merge PDFs Securely</a>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .page-header { padding: 80px 0 40px; background: var(--bg-subtle); text-align: center; }
    .content-section { padding: 60px 0; }
    .prose { line-height: 1.8; color: var(--slate); }
    .prose h2 { color: var(--dark); margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .container-narrow { max-width: 800px; }
</style>
